WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.920
This is how the trip would be made. Starship is&nbsp;
lifted into orbit by the Super Heavy booster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.780
which then comes back to Earth. It meets up with&nbsp;
another Starship configured as a tanker in order&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:14.940
to refuel an Earth's orbit before making the&nbsp;
long journey to the red planet. The booster isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.860
required for the return since there's no deep&nbsp;
gravity well to escape from on Mars. Starship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:25.980
flies solo, fueled by locally produced methane,&nbsp;
so the entire Starship system is fully reusable.

